id: pm-oqo9l2
title: "Episode identity: a stable, labelled, nestable episode key that survives process, surface and harness boundaries so trajectory grouping and fleet aggregation have a join key"
description: "First of the four seams pm-klxax7 owns, and the one it names its binding prerequisite. An episode spans several pm invocations across CLI, MCP and SDK surfaces, and the only per-session key recorded today is agent_instance, which is a harness-session identity rather than a task identity, is surface-dependent (pm-1zhfls: the MCP server does not receive the harness provenance environment, so one session records two identities), and is unlabelled (pm-rbg1qo: no role or topic has ever been recorded on any harness). Without a stable labelled key, pm-qd6gvf cannot group observation-action-outcome sequences and pm-gw6uyq cannot aggregate per run. Duplicate check: searched episode/session/trajectory/identity lineages, read pm-1zhfls (closed), pm-rbg1qo, pm-ffz0a9, pm-9wbiye, pm-li2fj5, pm-qd6gvf; the epic names this seam and no item owns it."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-environment,"area:sdk",provenance,rl
created_at: "2026-08-01T09:47:25.348Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T11:59:26.306Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T11:59:25.284Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T11:59:25.284Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "A declared episode key propagates unchanged across SDK, CLI and MCP invocations in one session; sub-episodes nest under their parent; each episode carries a declared label (role or topic); grouping trajectories by the key over a deliberately boundary-crossing episode returns exactly one episode with one nested child, order-independently; a workspace that never declares an episode records exactly what it records today and grouping falls back to the co-mutation inference marked as inferred; a missing key never fails, blocks or alters a mutation"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Give the agent-environment programme a join key that identifies an episode rather than a harness session
value: "Trajectory projection, fleet attribution and episode substrate all become groupable from the immutable record alone"
why_now: pm-klxax7 names this the programme's binding prerequisite and three filed features consume it without any of them being able to define it
parent: pm-klxax7
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Persist optional episode identity in immutable history and expose deterministic nested SDK grouping with legacy fallback.
expected_result: "Boundary-crossing mutations join one labelled episode with nested children, while undeclared work remains compatible."
actual_result: "Cross-surface episode propagation, nested parent inheritance, order-independent grouping, collision and cycle handling, and legacy inference all pass."
