close_reason: "Stable labelled nested episode identity and deterministic declared or inferred history grouping shipped across SDK, CLI, and MCP surfaces."
body: "## The seam\n\npm-klxax7 names this the programme's binding prerequisite: an episode spans several pm invocations, some through the CLI and some through MCP, and there is no key that identifies the episode across them. Without that key, trajectory projection (pm-qd6gvf) cannot group observation-action-outcome sequences, fleet attribution (pm-gw6uyq) cannot aggregate per-run, and the episode substrate (pm-li2fj5) has a unit with no identity.\n\nThe epic owns the seam. This item is the closeable tranche that delivers it.\n\n## What exists today, measured\n\nEvery history entry carries `agent_instance`, a per-session identifier assigned by harness detection. On a live claude-code session a mutation records:\n\n```\nauthor            harness:claude-code\nauthor_source     detected\nagent_harness     claude-code\nagent_instance    34ce3d428d5811b4f30f6318\nagent_provenance  { model: null, effort: { value: xhigh, source: environment }, role: null }\n```\n\n`agent_instance` is the closest thing to an episode key that exists, and it is not one, for three separate reasons.\n\nIt is a harness-session identity, not a task identity. One agent session that works three unrelated items produces one instance value spanning all three; three sessions that collaborate on one item produce three. Episodes and sessions are different partitions of the same event stream, and the substrate currently only records the second.\n\nIt is surface-dependent. pm-1zhfls established that the MCP server does not receive the harness provenance environment, so the same agent session records different provenance depending on whether a mutation went through the CLI or through a tool call. An episode that mixes both is recorded as two.\n\nIt is unlabelled. pm-rbg1qo established that no role or session topic has ever been recorded on any harness. Nothing in the record says what the episode was *for*, so grouping by instance yields anonymous partitions that a training or evaluation run cannot select on.\n\n## What the key has to be\n\nA first-class recorded dimension, not a derived heuristic. Co-mutation cohort inference (a pm-4k6b catalog entry) reconstructs plausible working sessions from mutation timing, and that is the right technique when nothing was declared — but an environment author knows the episode boundary exactly, and inferring what is known is a needless loss of precision. Both must exist: the declared key when present, the inference when absent.\n\nStable across process, surface, and harness. The same episode observed from a CLI invocation, an MCP tool call, and a direct SDK call must record the same key, which means the key propagates through the same channel discipline pm-ffz0a9 establishes for provenance rather than through a fourth ad-hoc mechanism.\n\nLabelled. An episode carries a declared purpose — role, topic, or task descriptor — because an unlabelled partition is not selectable, and selection is the entire point of recording it.\n\nNestable. A delegated sub-agent is a sub-episode of its parent; the environment `CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION` already distinguishes this in the environment today. A flat key cannot express a fleet where agents spawn agents, and a fleet where agents spawn agents is the target.\n\nNever load-bearing for correctness. A missing episode key degrades grouping; it must never fail a mutation, block a write, or change what is stored about the item itself.\n\n## Acceptance shape\n\nThe falsifier is a single episode that deliberately crosses every boundary: begun through the SDK, continued through two CLI invocations, continued through an MCP tool call, delegated to a sub-episode that mutates a different item, and ended. Projecting trajectories over the resulting history must return exactly one episode with one nested child, and grouping by the key must be byte-identical whether the projection reads the streams in file order or in timestamp order.\n\nThe degenerate case is equally binding: a workspace where no episode is ever declared must record exactly what it records today, with the inference path supplying grouping and marking it as inferred rather than declared.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nNot provenance channel design (pm-ffz0a9), which owns how a dimension is observed. This owns which dimension exists and what it identifies.\n\nNot dimension coverage per harness (pm-rbg1qo), which owns whether role and topic keys are declared for a given harness. This owns the episode as a unit, and consumes those keys as its label.\n\nNot trajectory projection (pm-qd6gvf) or the episode substrate (pm-li2fj5), both of which consume this key and neither of which can define it without duplicating the other."
